---
description: Folder layout, naming, and colocation for a maintainable React app
alwaysApply: true
---

# Structure

```
src/
  app/                 # router, providers, composition root
  pages/               # one file (or folder) per route, thin
  features/<name>/     # booking, rooms, guests, auth
    domain/
    application/
    data/
    ui/
  shared/
    ui/                # primitives (Button, Input, Stack)
    lib/               # dates, money, cn
    types/
  assets/
```

- Feature folders own their UI, hooks, tests, and types. Do not dump everything in `components/` or `utils/`.
- Files: `kebab-case.ts` / `kebab-case.tsx`. Components: `PascalCase` exports.
- Name by role: `room-list.tsx`, `use-room-search.ts`, `room-api.ts` — not `helpers.ts` or `data2.ts`.
- Colocate a module’s CSS (or `.module.css`) next to the component. Global tokens only in `src/shared` or `src/index.css`.
- Public API of a feature is `ui/` + application hooks. Other features import those, not `data/` internals.
- Keep files under ~200 lines. Split when a screen grows a form, a list, and a summary together.
- Tests sit beside the unit: `stay-total.test.ts` next to `stay-total.ts`.
